G0012.def:
ἄ-βυσσος, -ον (Ion. βυσσός = βυθός), 
__1. in cl., boundless, bottomless (e.g. ἄ. πέλαγος, ἄ. πλοῦτος Æsch.).
__2. [In LXX (for תְּהוֹם, Genèse 1:2, al.; exc. Ésaïe 44:27, Job 41:22 for צוּלָה, מְצוּלָה, Job 36:16 for רַחַב) and] NT, as subst. (MM, VGT, see word), ἡ ἄ. (sc. χώρα), the abyss; 
__(a) of the sea (Genèse 1:2); 
__(b) of the underworld, as the abode of the dead: Romains 10:7 (a paraphrase of Deutéronome 30:13 LXX); as the abode of demons, Luc 8:31, Apocalypse 9:1, 2, 11, 11:7, 17:8, 20:1, 3 (Cremer, 2). 
†

G0015.def:
ἀγαθὀ-ποιέω, -ῶ (= cl. ἀγαθὸν ποιεῖν, εὐεργετεῖν), 
[in LXX: Nombres 10:32, Juges 17:13 A, Sophonie 1:12 (יטב hi.), Tob.12:13 B, 1Ma.11:33, 2Ma.1:2 * ;] 
to do good; 
__(a) univ.: 1 Pierre 2:15, 20, 3:6, 17, 3Jo.11; 
__(b) for another's benefit: Marc 3:4 (T, ἀγαθὸν ποιῆσαι), Luc 6:9; 
__(with) accusative of person(s), Luc 6:33, 35 (Cremer, 8). 
†

G0021.def:
ἀγαλλιάω, -ῶ, Hellenistic form of cl. ἀγάλλω, to glorify, mid. -ομαι, to exult in; 
[in LXX (most frequently in Pss.) chiefly for גיל, רנן pi. ;] 
to exult, rejoice greatly: before ἐπί, with dative, Luc 1:47; with dative mod., 1 Pierre 1:8, Apocalypse 19:7. Mid., with same sense: Matthieu 5:12, Luc 10:21, Actes 2:26, 16:34, 1 Pierre 4:13; before ἵνα, Jean 8:56; ἐν, Jean 5:35 (1 aor. pass. perh. as mid.; but see Mozley, Psalter, 5), 1 Pierre 1:6 (Cremer, 590).†

G0027.def:
ἀγαπητός, -ή, -όν 
(ἀγαπάω), [in LXX chiefly for יָתִיד, יָדִיד ;] 
beloved (see M, Pr., 221); 
__(a) by God: of Christ, Matthieu 3:17; of men, Romains 1:7; 
__(b) by Christians, of one another: 1 Corinthiens 4:14; frequently as form of address, ib. 10:14; opposite to ἐχθρός, Romains 11:28 (see AR, Eph., 229; Cremer, 17; MM, VGT, see word).

G0048.def:
ἁγνίζω (> ἁγνός), 
[in LXX always ceremonially, chiefly for קָדַשׁ ;] 
to purify, cleanse from defilement; 
__(a) ceremonially: Jean 11:55, Actes 21:24, 26 24:18; 
__(b) morally: Jacques 4:8, 1 Pierre 1:22, 1 Jean 3:3.
† SYN.: καθαρίζω, which see (and see: ἁγνός).
